  "title": "Home",
  "text": "About me I am a Research Scholar at the Department of Applied Mechanics at IIT Delhi. My research focuses on crystal plasticity, finite element analysis and creep\u2013fatigue interaction. I work on decoding the complex mechanics of nickel-based superalloys using advanced frameworks such as MOOSE, to engineer a stronger and more resilient future. My work is multiscale, and the aim is to bridge the gap between the two scales. My current research interests include problems in the following areas: Dislocation density-based crystal plasticity Creep\u2013fatigue interaction in nickel-based superalloys Multiscale materials modelling High-temperature deformation of additively manufactured metals Damage modelling and life prediction My CV may be found here . Contact: Room 4A/14, Block IV, IIT Delhi, Hauz Khas, New Delhi 110016 Email: amz228601@iitd.ac.in Google Scholar Linkedin Github If you would like the models or the data behind the papers, please see Software ."
